meta {
  name: build code graph
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/codegraph/start
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}",
    "mode": "update",
    "provider": null,
    "model": null
  }
}

docs {
  Start graphify as a background job of the server against a session's working folder (card 472). mode full runs extract --code-only then cluster-only --no-label, which keeps the community names a graph already has; update runs update; with a provider, either then runs label --missing-only, which names only the communities without a name. provider is one of the harness providers the status lists (null for no labels) and model is required with it; both are checked before they become arguments. 202 started, 400 malformed or refused choice, 404 unknown session, 409 a build already runs for the folder, 503 graphify not installed.
  
  CAUTION: Runs graphify, which writes graphify-out/ into the session's folder and, with a provider, calls that model.
  
  Fence: host+origin+json. Loopback fence plus Origin check, and the request must carry Content-Type: application/json — anything else is 415.
  
  Writes state: yes
}
